  "Budget Direct, QBE and Kogan websites/PDS files return 403 to scrapers. Budget Direct and QBE limits come from their marketing pages, Finder/CHOICE and (QBE) the 2020 PDS QM8505-0620; the current QBE PDS is QM8505-1123 for policies from 1 Dec 2023.",
  "EV-specific wording: only Allianz (and Kogan, an Allianz white label, per CHOICE) explicitly covers the battery, thermal runaway and owned wall charger/cable. Youi explicitly says charging cables are NOT automatically covered. A&G and Hollard PDSs have no EV wording at all.",
  "Allianz new car replacement runs from manufacture date (2 years), not registration. A late-2025-built EX5 bought in 2026 gets less than 2 years. QBE (3 yrs / 60,000 km), Huddle Black (3 yrs) and Bupa Ultimate (3 yrs / 70,000 km) give the longest new car replacement in this group.",
  "Geely-specific price evidence: Youi publishes an EX5 comprehensive range of $1,082-$1,978/yr (80th percentile of policies sold 22 Nov 2025-22 May 2026). CHOICE (Jan 2026, 16,000+ EV quotes, all insurers) found Geely the cheapest EV brand to insure: $1,622 average for a new car vs $2,440 average for all new EVs, $2,220 for BYD and $2,985 for Tesla. Source: https://www.choice.com.au/money/insurance/car/articles/the-cost-of-insuring-electric-vehicles",
  "Market benchmarks: Canstar 2026 NSW average comprehensive premium $2,792 (up from $2,676 in 2025; 5-star policies average $1,991) https://www.canstar.com.au/news/car-insurance-costs-rev-up/ ; Finder NSW average $1,698 (via Mozo) https://www.mozo.com.au/car-insurance ; Compare the Market EV index avg $2,306 comprehensive (Mar 2026), MG4 Excite $1,524 (via Gridly) https://www.gridly.com.au/blog/ev-insurance-cost-australia/",
  "Awards context: Canstar 2026 Outstanding Value (national) went to AAMI, Bingle and ROLLiN', none in this group. Canstar 2026 Most Satisfied Customers: Bupa (national), ANZ (NSW), Youi (SA, WA). Finder 2026: Budget Direct won Best Value, Best Low Cost and Insurer of the Year; Youi won Best Features; ING, Qantas and Coles were each Highly Commended x3.",
  "No insurer-level claims acceptance or AFCA complaint data found for these brands. AFCA 2025-26: comprehensive motor was the most complained-about general insurance product (14,430 complaints, +28%).",
